=== task: mcq easy
title: The days of the week
prompt: A program stores one number for each day of the week. Which kind of array fits best?
* A static array of 7 items :: Right. The number of days never changes, so a fixed size is all you need.
- A dynamic array, so it can grow :: It would work, but there's nothing to grow: there are always 7 days.
- A 2D array :: There's only one value per day, so one row is enough.
- No array: the days can't be numbered :: Monday to Sunday can be indexes 0 to 6.
hint: Does the number of days ever change?
hint: A fixed number of items suits a fixed-size array.
right: A static array of 7 boxes: the size is known up front, and each day has its own index.
wrong: There are always exactly 7 days, so a static array of 7 items fits.

