=== task: cells medium
title: Moves for each insert
prompt: How many items move when you insert one new item into an array of 10 items, at each of these indexes?
labels: index 0 | index 3 | index 9 | index 10
answer: 10 | 7 | 1 | 0
wrong[9 | 6 | 0 | 0]: Inserting at index i moves the item already at i too: n − i items, not n − i − 1.
wrong[0 | 3 | 9 | 10]: It's the items **after** the index that move, so the front costs the most.
hint: Every item from index i to the end moves one box right.
hint: Moves = 10 − i.
