wrong: 10 − 0 = 10, 10 − 3 = 7, 10 − 9 = 1 and 10 − 10 = 0.

=== task: order medium
title: From cheapest to dearest
prompt: `arr` is an array of n items (sorted, where that matters). Put these in order, from the fewest steps to the most, for large n.
items:
- read item 5
- binary search for a value in the sorted array
- linear search for a value that isn't there
- insert n new items, each at the front
hint: Write each one in Big O.
hint: n inserts at the front move 0 + 1 + 2 + ... items.
right: O(1), O(log n), O(n) and O(n²). Inserting at the front one item at a time is the worst way to fill an array.
wrong: Reading is O(1), binary search O(log n), a failed linear search O(n), and n front inserts O(n²).

